# =============================================================================
# Konami System 573 - Quartus project (MiSTer / DE10-Nano, Cyclone V).
#
# Build (Quartus 17.0.2; see docs/DEPENDENCIES.md for the Colima/Docker recipe):
#   tools/apply_psx_patches.sh            # apply the psx/ EXP1 widening first
#   quartus_sh --flow compile Konami_System_573
#
# `sys/sys.tcl` (MiSTer framework) sets FAMILY/DEVICE, pulls sys.qip (which makes
# `sys_top` the real top and adds sys_top.sdc), and wires the PRE_FLOW build_id +
# the .sof->.rbf POST step. rtl/emu.sv (a clone of psx/PSX.sv with the 573 EXP1
# deltas) is the `emu` that sys_top instantiates.
# =============================================================================

set_global_assignment -name TOP_LEVEL_ENTITY sys_top
set_global_assignment -name ORIGINAL_QUARTUS_VERSION 17.0.2
set_global_assignment -name PROJECT_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY output_files

# Emit the MiSTer-loadable .rbf during assembly (upstream PSX.qsf sets this; the
# qsf bypasses sys/sys.tcl's post-flow, so wire the .rbf generation here instead).
set_global_assignment -name GENERATE_RBF_FILE ON

# The vendored PSX core is VHDL-2008 (psx_patches/0003 uses the 2008 `maximum()`);
# upstream sets this in psx/PSX.qsf. Required or the VHDL core won't analyze.
set_global_assignment -name VHDL_INPUT_VERSION VHDL_2008

# PSX_MiSTer needs the DDR3 framebuffer path (sys_top gates FB_* on this).
set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_MACRO "MISTER_FB=1"

# From the upstream PSX core's own PSX.qsf (psx/PSX.qsf, the build MiSTer ships with HDMI):
# nearest-neighbour instead of bilinear when the HDMI scaler DOWNscales, and no ALSA
# (Linux audio playback into the core's output -- unused here: the 573 MP3 reaches the
# mixer through its own DDR3 ring, rtl/s573_pcm_ring.v). Both only shrink the framework.
set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_MACRO "MISTER_DOWNSCALE_NN=1"
set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_MACRO "MISTER_DISABLE_ALSA=1"

# ????????????????????????????????????????????????????????? NO HDMI: analog / CRT-only build (2026-09-10) ?????????????????????????????????????????????????????????
# This project is used on a CRT over COMPOSITE, so the HDMI scaler is dead weight
# on a die at 100% LABs. MISTER_DEBUG_NOHDMI removes it, and the framework has 17
# guards plumbed for exactly this configuration (psx/sys/sys_top.v) -- it is a
# supported build, not a hack:
#     `ifdef MISTER_DEBUG_NOHDMI
#        wire vga_fb       = 0;
#        wire direct_video = 1;   -- native core timing straight to the analog out
#        wire vga_scaler   = 0;   -- no scaler on the analog path
# yc_out (the composite / S-video encoder) sits OUTSIDE the guard and is kept, as
# does the unscaled `vga_out vga_out` instance. So the CRT path survives intact and
# the scaled-VGA path -- which nothing here uses -- goes with the scaler.
#
# WHY IT MATTERS, and it is not mainly the area. The 2026-09-09 build closed timing
# at +0.006 ns, and the binding path was pll_hdmi (ascal). The next-worst SETUP path
# is emu|pll general[1] at +0.505 ns -- roughly 80x the margin. Removing the scaler
# should therefore turn "any added logic breaks the fit" into real headroom for the
# DDR Solo Select L/R inputs (already written, rtl/s573_io.v:143) and anything after
# them. Expected recovery from the June audit's per-entity table: ~2,256 ALM and
# ~25 DSP, which also lifts DSP off its 112/112 ceiling.
#
# WHAT IT COSTS: no HDMI output at all, and "Direct Video" is forced on rather than
# being an OSD choice. Both are what a 15 kHz CRT wants; neither is recoverable
# without a rebuild.
#
# HOW TO USE IT: this line is COMMENTED OUT, so the default build keeps HDMI.
# Do not edit it by hand -- `tools/build-573.ps1 -Crt` uncomments it for the
# duration of one compile and restores the file afterwards, so both variants are
# one flag apart from a single revision. Note psx_patches/0028
# (ascal bicubic off) becomes a no-op while this is enabled -- ascal is not
# instantiated at all -- but it is harmless and should stay for HDMI builds.
# Note also that SEED 3 was chosen upstream specifically to chase ascal's last
# 0.322 ns; with ascal gone that choice is arbitrary and worth re-rolling.
#
# UNTESTED as of this commit: upstream never built this configuration. Keep the
# known-good HDMI .rbf as a fallback before flashing a NOHDMI build.
# S573_CRT_MACRO (tools/build-573.ps1 -Crt toggles the next line; do not rename)
#set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_MACRO "MISTER_DEBUG_NOHDMI=1"
# 2: builds now run on the native dell box (i5-7500, 4 cores/4 threads, 14 GB RAM) --
# the Mac/Colima 11 GB VM that forced serial synthesis (6 workers OOM'd quartus_map) is
# gone. Under the hub's cap-2 build semaphore, 2 builds x 2 = 4 cores (full, no
# oversubscription); RAM-safe (A&S workers + Fitter peak ~4.6 GB << 14 GB). This only
# speeds Analysis & Synthesis + multi-corner timing (~6 min of ~38); the Fitter place &
# route -- the ~30 min / ~80% bottleneck -- is single-threaded regardless of this value.
# See docs/PHASE4_HARDWARE.md and memory dell-build-box (build-time levers).
# CHANGED 2 -> 1 (2026-09-09). On this build machine the Fitter died with an
# access violation inside the PARALLEL ROUTER:
#   l_run_heap_expansion_algorithm <- l_route_to_target <- l_route_net
#   <- aa_route_alg_route_all_nets <- l_rt_prl_worker      (quartus_fit.exe)
# Peak virtual memory 4609 MB -- i.e. exactly the ~4.6 GB Fitter peak the comment
# above records as normal. It is NOT an out-of-memory failure: the machine has
# 64 GB with 54 GB free at the time. (An earlier note here claimed an allocation
# failure; that was wrong. 4609 MB is evidence of NORMALITY, not of a ceiling --
# the Fitter used its usual memory and then faulted anyway.)
# What is left is a fault inside the PARALLEL router itself, with two threads on a
# design at the congestion ceiling. Serial routing removes the faulting code path.
# Note the comment above is wrong that the Fitter is single-threaded regardless of
# this value: the fault is in l_rt_prl_worker, a parallel ROUTING worker.
set_global_assignment -name NUM_PARALLEL_PROCESSORS 1

# Core RTL (573 fabric + emu.sv + the nested psx/rtl PSX core qips).
set_global_assignment -name QIP_FILE files.qip
set_global_assignment -name SEARCH_PATH rtl

# MiSTer framework: use the PSX core's OWN sys (psx/sys), NOT the repo's sys/.
# emu.sv is a clone of psx/PSX.sv, which targets the (older) Template version in
# psx/sys -- the repo's newer sys/ packs HPS_BUS differently (no fb_en/sl), which
# fails to elaborate against emu.sv. psx/sys/sys.qip is qip-path-relative so it
# resolves its own files correctly (the sys HDL + sys_top.sdc), and it provides
# pll_q17 (= the `pll` PSX.sv instantiates). Device assignments are identical
# between the two sys.tcl files.
set_global_assignment -name FAMILY "Cyclone V"
set_global_assignment -name DEVICE 5CSEBA6U23I7
set_global_assignment -name DEVICE_FILTER_PACKAGE UFBGA
set_global_assignment -name DEVICE_FILTER_PIN_COUNT 672
set_global_assignment -name DEVICE_FILTER_SPEED_GRADE 7
set_global_assignment -name PRE_FLOW_SCRIPT_FILE "quartus_sh:psx/sys/build_id.tcl"
set_global_assignment -name QIP_FILE psx/sys/sys.qip

# Board PIN assignments. CRITICAL: sys.qip carries the framework HDL + SDC but NO
# pin locations -- those live in psx/sys/sys.tcl + sys_analog.tcl, which upstream
# psx/PSX.qsf `source`s but we can't (their relative file-refs resolve wrong from
# our root and would re-pull the incompatible repo sys/). sys_pins.tcl is the pin
# locations only, extracted from those two files. Without it every board pin
# (SDRAM, HDMI, VGA, ...) auto-places to an arbitrary ball -> SDRAM dead (BIOS
# can't run) and VGA on wrong pins (CRT can't lock). See sys_pins.tcl header.
source sys_pins.tcl

# Timing constraints for the PSX core's video PLL. CRITICAL: psx/PSX.sdc is the
# ONLY place the pll2 -> clk_vid divide-by-5 create_generated_clock and the cross-
# PLL false-paths (pll<->pll2, FPGA_CLK<->pll2, pll_hdmi<->pll2, h2f<-pll2) live.
# sys.qip only brings sys_top.sdc (no pll2/clk_vid). Without PSX.sdc those video
# pixel-clock domain crossings are unconstrained and STA reports large negative
# slack on the core clocks (clk_1x cannot even close to its ~33.8 MHz) -- i.e.
# "0 A&S errors" but a TIMING-FAILED bitstream that misbehaves on silicon. The
# instance paths (emu|pll2|..., emu|pll|..., pll_hdmi|..., sysmem|...) match our
# sys_top->emu hierarchy (emu.sv is the PSX.sv clone). Read AFTER sys_top.sdc.
set_global_assignment -name SDC_FILE psx/PSX.sdc
# 573-specific constraints (false path on the compiled-out savestate read bus). Read LAST.
set_global_assignment -name SDC_FILE Konami_System_573.sdc

set_global_assignment -name LAST_QUARTUS_VERSION "17.0.2 Lite Edition"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fitter effort (2026-07-30). The project ran on Quartus DEFAULTS until now
# (Balanced, no physical synthesis, seed 1). The one timing failure we carry is
# ascal's HDMI output address generation -- a THREE-logic-level path missing
# setup by ~2.2 ns on the 148.5 MHz pixel clock, measured identically before and
# after the P4b MP3 slices (-2.216 vs -2.143), so it is congestion/placement, not
# design. Three levels missing by 2.2 ns is the profile a fitter can often close
# on its own, and it is worth trying BEFORE spending the remaining ALM levers,
# which are now all high-risk (mdec / gte / savestate -- the cheap ones were
# already taken by psx_patches 0025/0026/0027).
#
# "High Performance Effort" rather than "Aggressive Performance" on purpose: the
# die is at 100% LAB occupancy, and the aggressive mode trades area for speed,
# which here risks not fitting at all. Physical synthesis is limited to combo
# logic + register duplication for the same reason -- both are targeted at
# critical paths rather than global area growth.
#
# If this does not move the ascal slack materially, the number is structural and
# the next step is characterising seed variance, NOT more effort.
set_global_assignment -name OPTIMIZATION_MODE "High Performance Effort"
set_global_assignment -name PHYSICAL_SYNTHESIS_COMBO_LOGIC ON
# HDMI M2 experiment (2026-10-18): M1 (HDMI in) placed at 41,478 ALM / 100% LABs and failed to
# route. Register duplication cost ~1,200 ALM when it was added (2026-07-30 table above);
# M2 measures the area it costs now, with upstream PSX.qsf's COMBO_LOGIC_FOR_AREA instead.
set_global_assignment -name PHYSICAL_SYNTHESIS_REGISTER_DUPLICATION ON
set_global_assignment -name PHYSICAL_SYNTHESIS_COMBO_LOGIC_FOR_AREA ON

# MEASURED (2026-07-30): the two settings above took the ascal HDMI setup slack
# from -2.143 ns to -0.322 ns and total negative slack from -55.6 to -4.9 -- i.e.
# 85% of the shortfall was the project sitting on Quartus DEFAULTS, not
# congestion. Cost: 39,157 -> 40,367 ALMs (93% -> 96%), which is physical
# synthesis duplicating registers to shorten paths. Still fits, still produces an
# rbf.
#
# Chasing the last 0.322 ns with a placement SEED rather than more optimization
# effort, deliberately: at 96% ALM occupancy the remaining effort levers
# (Aggressive Performance, register retiming) all buy speed with AREA, and there
# is not much area left. A seed is area-neutral -- it just re-rolls placement,
# and 0.3 ns is well inside normal seed spread.
# SEED 3 -> 4 (2026-09-28): with the DIO write-pointer export in, seed 3 closed setup
# (+0.836) but missed HOLD by 0.338 ns on the vendored sdram.sv 3x->1x
# dma_reqprocessed sync -- a path nothing in this tree touches; ALL PATHS hold
# padding did not catch it at 99 % LABs. Seed 4: +0.495 setup / +0.061 hold, clean.
# SEED 4 -> 5 (2026-10-02): re-rolled after quartus_fit died in the router twice on seed 4
# (jobs 213/216). Not shown to be seed-related: job 218 on seed 5 then lost quartus_sta to
# an access violation too, and STA passed when re-run alone. See
# docs/2026-10-02-review-steps-2-3.md.
set_global_assignment -name SEED 5
# HOLD (2026-09-18). Quartus's default OPTIMIZE_HOLD_TIMING covers only I/O and
# minimum-tPD paths, so an internal register-to-register hold violation is left
# standing: build #2 of the pcprof/MDEC A/B bitstream had exactly one, -0.256 ns
# on savestates SS_DataRead[27] (clk_1x) -> SS_DataRead_2x[27] (clk_2x), with
# setup clean everywhere. ALL PATHS lets the fitter pad such paths with routing
# delay. Area-neutral in principle (delay, not logic).
set_global_assignment -name OPTIMIZE_HOLD_TIMING "ALL PATHS"